robin <usenet@unrated.net> writes:

[about the logmoves patch]

> This patch would allow us to do a "Fastest Ascension" trophy, but only
> in terms of gametime. It's been suggested that a matching trophy for
> realtime would also be good.
> Would it be particularly difficult to get the logfile to store yyyymmddhhmmss,
> instead of just yyyymmdd?

You would probably need to change the toptenentry struct defined at about
line 43 of topten.c. It now stores deathdate and birthdate as long, and
the value is the numerical value you see in the logfile. Then you would
need to update all references to it. Probably not particularly difficult,
but.. there is not very much time left before the tournament should start,
and we don't want to change it DURING the tournament because it would
break logfile and record compatibility.. the change would need to be
tested thoroughly and compiled in on every tournament machine during the
weekend.

I'm sure I don't have time for making and testing the change because I
have other plans for the weekend. Somebody else might have the time, but I
doubt it with this schedule, for this year's tournament. But maybe next
year. 

